  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation, reaching 0.653 accuracy and 0.628 F1, clearly ahead of PCA and scGPT settings. Image-only ResNet50 is weak, especially single-profile, so the key uncertainty is whether image features can add complementary value to the strong RNA representation. config_033 keeps the best RNA design fixed and adds ResNet50 image features with weighted fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion improves over the RNA-only baseline while allowing the weak image modality to be downweighted. It is the best next use of budget because it is a minimal, logical extension of the current best direction, avoids confounding with the untested ViT image encoder, and will clarify whether further multimodal or image-encoder exploration is worthwhile."
}

